# Screen display breakpoints

Use **Bootstrap 5** mobile-first breakpoints for storefront CSS, Tailwind screens, admin preview, and any new responsive UI.

Source of truth: `lib/breakpoints.ts` + Tailwind `theme.screens` in `tailwind.config.js` (must stay in sync with this rule).

## Breakpoints + container max-width

| Name | Devices | Min width | Container max-width |
|------|---------|-----------|---------------------|
| `xs` | portrait phones | &lt;576px (default) | none (auto / 100%) |
| `sm` | landscape phones | ≥576px | 540px |
| `md` | tablets | ≥768px | 720px |
| `lg` | desktops | ≥992px | 960px |
| `xl` | large desktops | ≥1200px | 1140px |
| `xxl` | larger desktops | ≥1400px | 1320px |

## Media queries (mobile-first)

```css
/* X-Small — portrait phones, less than 576px
   No media query for xs — this is the default */

/* Small — landscape phones, 576px and up */
@media (min-width: 576px) { ... }

/* Medium — tablets, 768px and up */
@media (min-width: 768px) { ... }

/* Large — desktops, 992px and up */
@media (min-width: 992px) { ... }

/* X-Large — large desktops, 1200px and up */
@media (min-width: 1200px) { ... }

/* XX-Large — larger desktops, 1400px and up */
@media (min-width: 1400px) { ... }
```

In Tailwind use: `sm:` `md:` `lg:` `xl:` `xxl:` / `2xl:` (both map to 1400px). Do **not** use Tailwind’s default 640/1024/1280/1536 scale.

## Admin preview mapping

| Preview switcher | Breakpoint | Frame width |
|------------------|------------|-------------|
| Mobile | `xs` | 390px |
| Tablet | `md` | 768px |
| Desktop | `lg`+ | full preview pane |

Inside admin preview frames, use `previewViewport` helpers (`lib/preview-viewport.ts`) — browser media queries still follow the **window**, not the frame.

## Equal left / right fit (required)

Every storefront screen and admin preview frame must look **professionally balanced**: left and right gaps match, content sits centered in the available width, and no side looks tighter or looser than the other.

**Mandatory checks** (storefront + admin preview: mobile / tablet / desktop):

1. Measure or visually confirm **left inset = right inset** for each content section.
2. Sections on the same page share the same horizontal rhythm (do not mix `px-[5px]`, `p-[10px]`, asymmetric `pl-*` / `pr-*`, or one-sided margins).
3. Grids/rows must not push content off one edge (watch Bootstrap negative gutters, `w-max`, absolute children, closed flyouts).
4. Full-bleed bands (hero, trust banner) stay edge-to-edge; their **inner** text/media still uses equal L/R if inset.

**Implementation**

- Use `STORE_SECTION_EDGE_X_CLASS` (`px-4 sm:px-6`) or `STORE_SECTION_EDGE_CLASS` (same X + vertical) from `lib/breakpoints.ts` for cards, tabs, collections list, pagination, footer, and any new content section.
- Match header / announcement / desktop nav horizontal padding (`px-4 sm:px-6`).
- Never pad or margin only one side for section layout. Never invent one-off edge px values that break alignment across sections.

## Layout rules

- Mobile-first: base = `xs`; enhance from `sm` → `xxl`.
- Contained content: use container max-widths above (or Bootstrap `container` / `bootstrap-grid`).
- Full-bleed (hero, trust banner bands, dividers): `width: 100%`; inner content may use the same edge class when needed.
- Never invent custom breakpoint px values that conflict with this table.
- Collection product-count badge matches product card New/Sale badge styling (`absolute right-2 top-2 rounded bg-gray-900 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-wide text-white`); do not size it with breakpoints or `vw`.
